"hadiths[30]{hadithnumber,text}:"
1175,"Yunus bin Jubair said:""I asked Ibn Umar about a man who divorced his wife while she was menstruating. So he said: 'Don't you know Abdullah bin Umar?' Indeed he divorced his wife while she was menstruating"
1176,"Salim narrated that:His father divorced his wife during her menses"
1177,"# Translation of the Hadith

**Narrated by Mu'adh ibn Jabal (may Allah be pleased with him), who reported that the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said:**

""No woman harms her husband in this worldly life except that his wife among the *Hoor al-'Een* (companions of Paradise) says: 'Do not harm him! May Allah fight you! He is merely a guest (*dakheel*) in your company, and it is near that he will leave you and come to us.'""

**Abu 'Eesaa (al-Tirmidhi) said:** ""This is a *hasan gharib* (good yet rare) Hadith. We do not know it except through this chain of narration. The narration of Isma'il ibn 'Ayyash from the people of Shaam (Greater Syria) is more sound (*aslah*), whereas his narrations from the people of Hijaz and the people of Iraq contain *manakeer* (objectionable reports).""

---

## Notes on Translation

- **"
1178,"Narrated Qutaybah ibn Sa'id, narrated Hammad ibn Zayd, from Ayyub, from Muhammad ibn Sirin, from Yunus ibn Jubayr, who said: I asked Ibn 'Umar رضي الله عنهما about a man who divorced his wife while she was in a state of menstruation. He said: ""Do you know 'Abdullah ibn 'Umar? He divorced his wife while she was in a state of menstruation, so 'Umar رضي الله عنه asked the Prophet ﷺ, and he commanded him to take her back."" He said: I said, ""Is that divorce counted?"" He said, ""What then? What if he was unable to do so and acted foolishly?"""
1179,"Fatimah bint Qais said:""My husband divorced me three times during the time of the Prophet. So the Messenger of Allah said: 'There is no housing for you nor maintenance.'"" Al-Mughirah (one of the narrators) said: ""I mentioned that to Ibrahim and he said: Umar said: ""We do not leave the Book of Allah and the Sunnah of our Prophet for the saying of a woman"
1180,"# Translation of the Hadith

**Hannād narrated to us:** Qabīṣah narrated to us, from Jarīr ibn Ḥāzim, from al-Zubayr ibn Saʿīd, from ʿAbdullāh ibn Yazīd ibn Rukānah, from his father, from his grandfather, who said:

""I came to the Prophet ﷺ and said, 'O Messenger of Allāh, I have pronounced *al-battah* (irrevocable) divorce upon my wife.' He ﷺ said, **'What did you intend by it?'** I said, 'One (divorce).' He ﷺ said, **'By Allāh?'** I said, 'By Allāh.' He ﷺ said, **'Then it is what you intended.'**

Abū ʿĪsā (al-Tirmidhī) said: *This is a ḥadīth that we do not know except through this chain of narration. I asked Muḥammad (i.e., Imām al-Bukhārī) about this ḥadīth, and he said there is idṭirāb (discrepancy) in it.*

It is narrated from ʿIkrimah, from Ibn ʿAbbās"
1181,"Muzahir bin Aslam narrated that Al-Qasim narrated from Aishah that:The Messenger of Allah said: ""The divorce for a slave woman is two divorces"
1182,"Abu Hurairah narraed that:The Messenger of Allah said: ""Allah has permitted my Ummah what occurs in their mines"
1183,"Hannad narrated to us, Jarir narrated to us, from Mughirah, from Ash-Sha'bi who said: ""Fatimah bint Qais said: 'My husband divorced me with three (divorces) during the time of the Prophet (ﷺ), so the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: ""There is no lodging for you and no maintenance.""'"" Mughirah said: ""So I mentioned it to Ibrahim, and he said: 'Umar said: ""We will not abandon the Book of Allah and the Sunnah of our Prophet (ﷺ) for the statement of a woman - we do not know whether she remembered or forgot."" And Umar used to grant her lodging and maintenance.

Ahmad bin Mani' narrated to us, Hushaim narrated to us, Husain, Isma'il and Mujalid informed us - Hushaim said - and Dawud also narrated to us, from Ash-Sha'bi who said: ""I went to Fatimah bint Qais and asked her about the ruling of the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) concerning her. She said: 'Her husband divorced her irrevocably, so she disputed with him about the lodging and maintenance, but the Prophet (ﷺ) did not grant her lodging or maintenance.'"" And in the Hadith of Dawud, she said: ""And he commanded me to spend my waiting period in the house of Ibn Umm Maktum.""

Abu Eisa said: This Hadith is Hasan Sahih. And it is the view of some of the people of knowledge, among them Al-Hasan Al-Basri, 'Ata' bin Abi Rabah, and Ash-Sha'bi. Ahmad and Ishaq also hold this view. They say: ""There is no lodging or maintenance for the divorced woman if her husband does not have the right to take her back."" And some of the people of knowledge among the Companions of the Prophet (ﷺ), among them 'Umar and 'Abdullah, said: ""The woman who is divorced with three (divorces) has lodging and maintenance."" This is the view of Sufyan Ath-Thawri and the people of Al-Kufah. And some of the people of knowledge said: ""She has lodging but no maintenance."" This is the view of Malik bin Anas, Al-Laith bin Sa'd, and Ash-Shafi'i. Ash-Shafi'i said: ""We only granted her lodging on the basis of the Book of Allah. Allah Most High said: 'Do not turn them out of their houses, nor should they (themselves) leave, unless they commit an open lewdness.'"" They said this refers to abusive speech - that she is abusive to her husband's family. And he argued that the Prophet (ﷺ) did not grant Fatimah bint Qais lodging because she used to be abusive to her husband's family. Ash-Shafi'i said: ""And she has no maintenance, based on the Hadith of the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) in the story of Fatimah bint Qais."""
1184,"AR-Rubayyi bint Mu'awwidh bin Al-Afra narrated:that she got a Khul during the time of the Prophet. So the Prophet ordered her - or: she was ordered - that she observe an Iddah of a menstruation"
1185,"Yunus bin Jubair said:""I asked Ibn Umar about a man who divorced his wife while she was menstruating. So he said: 'Don't you know Abdullah bin Umar?' Indeed he divorced his wife while she was menstruating"
1186,"Thawban narrated that :The Messenger of Allah said: ""Whichever woman seeks a Khul from her husband without harm (cause)"
1187,"Abu Hurairah narrated that:The Messenger of Allah said: ""Indeed the woman is like a rib"
1188,"# Translation of the Hadith

**Narrated by Mahmūd ibn Ghaylān**, who reported from **al-Faḍl ibn Mūsā**, from **Sufyān**, from **Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān**, the freed slave of the family of Ṭalḥah, from **Sulaymān ibn Yasār**, from **al-Rubayyiʿ bint Muʿawwidh ibn ʿAfrāʾ** (may Allāh be pleased with her), that she sought a *khulʿ* (divorce initiated by the wife) during the time of the Prophet ﷺ. The Prophet ﷺ commanded her — or she was commanded — to observe her *ʿiddah* (waiting period) with **one menstrual cycle**.

He (Abū ʿĪsā) said: ""In this chapter, there is also a narration from Ibn ʿAbbās (may Allāh be pleased with him).""

Abū ʿĪsā (al-Tirmidhī) said: ""The authentic narration from al-Rubayyiʿ (may Allāh be pleased with her) is that she was commanded to observe her *ʿiddah* with one menstrual cycle.""

---

**Source:** *Jāmiʿ al-Tirmidhī*"
1189,"Abu Hurairah narrated that:The Prophet said: ""No woman should ask for the divorce of her sister (in religion) in order to spill what is in her container"
1190,"Abu Hurairah narrated that :The Messenger of Allah said: ""Every divorce is valid except the divorce of the Ma'tuh person whose reason is overcome."" (Da'if Jiddan)"
1191,"# Translation of the Hadith

**Bundār informed us** that ʿAbd al-Wahhāb informed us that Ayyūb informed us from Abū Qilābah, from the one who narrated to him from Thawbān رضي الله عنه that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said:

> **""Any woman who asks her husband for a divorce without any valid cause, the fragrance of Paradise shall be forbidden unto her.""**

Abū ʿĪsā (al-Tirmidhī) said: **""This is a ḥasan (good) Hadith.""**

He further noted: **""This Hadith is also narrated from Ayyūb, from Abū Qilābah, from Abū Asmāʾ, from Thawbān رضي الله عنه.""**

He added: **""Some of them narrated it from Ayyūb through this chain of transmission (isnād) but did not raise it (to the level of a Prophetic statement, i.e., they stopped it as a statement of a Companion).""**

---

*This Hadith is recorded in Sunan al-Tirmidhī and underscores the gravity of a wife seeking divorce from her husband without a legitimate sharʿī reason, as it constitutes a serious matter in the sight of Allah ﷻ.*"
1192,"Al-Aswad narrated from Abu As-Sanabil bin Ba'kak who said:""Subai'ah delivered twenty-three or twenty-five days after her husband had died. So when she was ready (finished post-natal bleeding) she adorned herself for marriage"
1193,"# Hadith Translation

**Narrated to us Ahmad ibn Muhammad, that he was informed by Ibn al-Mubarak, who was informed by Ibn Abi Dhi'b, from Al-Harith ibn 'Abd al-Rahman, from Hamzah ibn 'Abd Allah ibn 'Umar, from Ibn 'Umar (may Allah be pleased with him), who said:**

*""There was a woman under my marriage whom I loved, but my father [i.e., 'Umar ibn al-Khattab] disliked her. My father commanded me to divorce her, but I refused. I mentioned this to the Prophet ﷺ, and he said: **'O 'Abd Allah ibn 'Umar, divorce your wife.'**""*

Abu 'Isa [al-Tirmidhi] commented: *""This is a hasan sahih hadith. We only know it through the narration of Ibn Abi Dhi'b.""*

---

**Notes on the Translation:**

- **""Under my marriage""** (تَحْتِي): An idiomatic expression in classical Arabic denoting a wife or spouse under one's marital bond.
- **""My father""** refers to **'Umar ibn al-Khattab** (may Allah be pleased with him), the second Caliph of Islam, as Ibn 'Umar's father.
- The Prophet ﷺ is reported to have said: **يَا عَبْدَ اللَّهِ بْنَ عُمَرَ طَلِّقِ"
1194,"Humaid bin Nafi narrated that :Zainab bint Abi Salamah said: ""I entered upon Umm Habibah"
1195,"Humaid bin Nafi narrated that :Zainab said: ""So I entered upon Zainab bint Jahsh when her brother died. She called for some perfume and put it on"
1196,"Humaid bin Nafi narrated that :Zainab said: ""And I heard my mother"
1197,"Narrated to us Ahmad ibn Mani', narrated to us Husayn ibn Muhammad, narrated to us Shayban, from Mansur, from Ibrahim, from al-Aswad, from Abu al-Sanabil ibn Ba'kak, who said:

Subay'a gave birth twenty-three or twenty-five days after the death of her husband. When she had recovered (from childbirth), she adorned herself for marriage, and this was disapproved of. The matter was mentioned to the Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him, who said: **""If she does so, then her waiting period has indeed ended.""**

Narrated to us Ahmad ibn Mani', narrated to us al-Hasan ibn Musa, narrated to us Shayban, from Mansur, a similar narration.

He (al-Tirmidhi) said: And in this chapter there is also a narration from Umm Salamah, may Allah be pleased with her.

Abu 'Isa (al-Tirmidhi) said: The hadith of Abu al-Sanabil is a well-known hadith from this chain. And we do not know of al-Aswad having heard directly from Abu al-Sanabil. And I heard Muhammad (al-Bukhari) say: ""I do not know that Abu al-Sanabil lived after the Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him.""

And the practice (established ruling) according to the majority of the people of knowledge from among the Companions of the Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him, and others is that a pregnant woman whose husband has passed away — when she gives birth, marriage becomes permissible for her, even if her full waiting period has not yet elapsed. This is the position of Sufyan al-Thawri, al-Shafi'i, Ahmad, and Ishaq.

And some of the people of knowledge from among the Companions of the Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him, and others said: She must observe the longer of the two periods (i.e., either the waiting period of four months and ten days or until childbirth, whichever is later). And the first opinion is the more correct."
1198,"# Translation of the Hadith

**Qutaybah narrated to us, al-Layth narrated to us, from Yaḥyā ibn Saʿīd, from Sulaymān ibn Yasār, that Abū Hurayrah, Ibn ʿAbbās, and Abū Salamah ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān discussed the matter of a pregnant woman whose husband had passed away and she gave birth at the time of her husband's death.**

**Ibn ʿAbbās, may Allah be pleased with him, said:** ""She must observe the longer of the two waiting periods (*ʿiddah*).""

**Abū Salamah, may Allah be pleased with him, said:** ""Rather, she becomes permissible (for remarriage) as soon as she gives birth.""

**Abū Hurayrah, may Allah be pleased with him, said:** ""I agree with my nephew,"" meaning Abū Salamah.

**So they sent a message to Umm Salamah, the wife of the Prophet ﷺ, and she said:** ""Subayʿah al-Aslamiyyah, may Allah be pleased with her, gave birth shortly after the death of her husband, so she sought a ruling from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and he commanded her to remarry.""

**Abū ʿĪsā (al-Tirmidhī) said:** ""This is a *ḥasan ṣaḥīḥ* hadith.""

---

### Notes on Key Terms:

- **"
1199,"Abu Salamah and Muhammad bin Abdur-Rahman (bin Thawban) narrated that :Salman bin Sakhr Al-Ansari - from Banu Bayadah - said that his wife was like the back of his mother to him until Ramadan passed. After half of Ramadan had passed he had intercourse with his wife during the night. So he went to the Messenger of Allah to mention that to him. The Messenger of Allah said to him: ""Free a slave."" He said: ""I don't have one."" So he said: ""Then fast two consecutive months."" He said: ""I am unable."" He said: ""Feed sixty needy people."" He said: ""I can not."" So the Messenger of Allah said to Farwah bin Amr: ""Give him that Araq - and it is a large basket that holds fifteen or sixteen Sa - to feed sixty needy people"
1200,"Aishah narrated:""The Messenger of Allah swore Ila from his wives"
1201,"Sa'eed bin Jubair narrated:""I was asked about those who were involved in the case of Li'an and if they are to be separated"
1202,"Abū Saʿīd al-Ashajj narrated to us, ʿAbdullāh ibn Idrīs narrated to us, from Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq, from Muḥammad ibn ʿAmr ibn ʿAṭāʾ, from Sulaymān ibn Yasār, from Salamah ibn Ṣakhr al-Bayāḍī, from the Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him, regarding the one who commits ẓihār and then has intercourse before expiating, he said: ""A single expiation."" Abū ʿĪsā said: This is a ḥasan gharīb hadith. The practice according to this is held by the majority of the scholars, and it is the view of Sufyān al-Thawrī, Mālik, al-Shāfiʿī, Aḥmad, and Isḥāq. Some of them said: If he has intercourse before expiating, then upon him are two expiations. This is the view of ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Mahdī."
1203,"Zainab bint Ka'b bin Ujrah narrated that :Al-Furay'ah bint Malik bin Sinan - the sister of the Abu Sa'eed Al-Khudri - informed her that she went to the Messenger of Allah to ask him if she could return to her family in Banu Khudrah. Her husband had gone out searching for his runaway slaves"
1204,"Ibn Mas'ud narrated:""The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) cursed the one who consumed Riba"
